 "translation": "Kishwar, my Kishwar, I cried out involuntarily, and the next moment the door curtain was pulled aside, and for a little while all my strength was drained. In the middle of the room, a little away from a cupboard, Kishwar was slumped like a dead bird in Shaukat's terrifying and cruel arms. And you could say that, have you ever seen a pigeon feeding its young? Exactly like that. The next moment, Shaukat was scratching his head, looking at the blending of colors in the picture hanging nearby, and Kishwar was quickly opening and closing her purse. Her eyes were downcast and her face was red. \"This... this is Shaukat, Rehana... Shaukat,\" Kishwar was saying.",
